{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevHNNY6hrZ4zzMiFMcZ5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## ANALYSIS SUMMARY\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:** Add a POST endpoint at `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status (idempotent for retries), rejects CANCELLED shipments with HTTP 409, and returns 404 for unknown shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14` with `ShipmentStatus` enum at line 23-27\n- Repository: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` with in-memory store\n- Controller: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` using `@RestController` and `@PostMapping`/`@GetMapping`\n- Error handling: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` defines `ResourceNotFoundException` and `ConflictException`\n- Error codes: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` defines enum with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`, `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`, etc.\n- Exception handler: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` converts exceptions to `ApiError` responses\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409) rather than building responses\n2. Error codes are defined in a closed enum in `ApiError.kt` and must be added deliberately\n3. Tests use MockMvc with `jsonPath` assertions on both status and error response structure\n4. The repository provides `findById`, `existsById`, and `save` methods for data operations\n5. POST endpoints that create resources return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED)` (201), but for state transitions they likely return 200 OK\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — add the confirm endpoint (cannot be avoided)\n2. `ApiError.kt` — add new error code for invalid shipment status (required for 409 responses on CANCELLED shipments)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add test cases covering all scenarios (cannot be avoided)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. If I misunderstand the idempotent requirement: retrying confirm on a CONFIRMED shipment must return 200, not 409\n2. Concurrency: the in-memory store uses ConcurrentHashMap but the read-modify-write isn't atomic—though tests don't verify this\n3. The new error code must be added to the enum which changes the API contract\n\n**Open questions:**\n1. For a CANCELLED shipment rejection, should I reuse `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` or add a new error code? The requirement says HTTP 409 (Conflict) but doesn't specify the code. Since `ALREADY_EXISTS` is semantically wrong, I need a new code. Likely name: `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` or `INVALID_SHIPMENT_STATE_TRANSITION`. No decision needed before DESIGN; conventions suggest domain-specific codes.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the `ErrorCode` enum to distinguish the state transition error from existing conflict codes. This allows clients to branch on this specific failure in their retry logic.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** — Add a new endpoint:\n   - Route: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Logic:\n     - Find the shipment by `shipmentId` → if not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException` with code `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` (returns 404)\n     - If status is `CREATED` → update to `CONFIRMED`, save, return 200 OK with the updated shipment\n     - If status is `CONFIRMED` → no change, return 200 OK with the unchanged shipment (idempotent retry)\n     - If status is `CANCELLED` → throw `ConflictException` with code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` (returns 409)\n   - Return type: `Shipment` directly (spring serializes to JSON automatically)\n   - HTTP status: 200 OK for success cases, 409 for CANCELLED, 404 for not found\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment to confirmed status` — verify transition and persistence\n   - `idempotent confirm of already confirmed shipment` — confirm twice, verify second returns same state\n   - `rejects confirm of cancelled shipment with 409` — verify ConflictException and error code\n   - `rejects confirm of unknown shipment with 404` — verify ResourceNotFoundException and error code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered adding a service layer (`ShipmentService`) between the controller and repository, but the existing controllers (`OrderController`, `ShipmentController`) operate directly on repositories. Adding a service layer would be unrelated refactoring per the boundaries and would diverge from existing conventions.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Caller receives | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|-----------------|-----------|\n| Unknown shipment | Find by ID returns null | (none) | 404 + error envelope | `ResourceNotFoundException` → `GlobalExceptionHandler` |\n| Confirm CREATED | Read shipment with status=CREATED | Update to CONFIRMED, save | 200 + updated Shipment JSON | `save()` to repository, return Shipment |\n| Retry CONFIRMED | Read shipment with status=CONFIRMED | (none, save unchanged) | 200 + same Shipment JSON | Read current state, return as-is |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | Read shipment with status=CANCELLED | (none) | 409 + error envelope | `ConflictException` → `GlobalExceptionHandler` |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n| Test | Scenario | Validates |\n|------|----------|-----------|\n| `confirms a created shipment` | Create S-1, confirm, verify | Status transitions to CONFIRMED and persists |\n| `idempotent confirm` | Create, confirm, confirm again | Second call returns 200 with CONFIRMED, no error |\n| `rejects cancelled` | Create, manually set to CANCELLED, confirm | Returns 409 with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` code |\n| `rejects unknown` | Confirm non-existent S-missing | Returns 404 with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` code |\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2546,"cache_read_input_tokens":21046,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2546},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0d20b8c-d4a7-414c-924b-eb25719789a5","uuid":"20568230-f9cf-4ca8-bf3a-c355ed8bd668","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:07:25.291Z","request_id":"req_011CevHNMtQVsyCNsqH2aZTR"}
